B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m9\u001b[11G\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m50\u001b[11G\u001b[22mok\u001b[14G= np.isfinite(meas)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0Allowed by auto mode\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf  $ cat > reconcile/r6b_check.py <<'EOF'\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B#!/usr/bin/env python3\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;5;246m\"\"\"R6b:\u001b[14Gis\u001b[17Gthe measured boundary self-consistent, and who is right about the 6 s offset?\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BE029 recorded the analyst's finding that data/steps.csv t_start was LATE by 6.34 s, and both nodes\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;246mshifted their boundaries earlier by about that mu\u2026\r\u001b[12C\u001b[2BChecking\u001b[22Gfilesystem traversal scope\u2026 \u00b7 5m 58s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[63G24.5k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[31;3H\u001b[?25h"]
